From: mscharged-port native source preparation
Subject: [PATCH] Deliver pending native PE finish before the SDK reset section
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

The real original loading path exposed an already-completed older finish
latched for48ms while source aperture stores ran. The next GXSetDrawDone reset
then owner-delivered that older cause in its wait, before its own XFB copy
completed. A four-pass chain stayed one genuine finish behind; VI correctly
rejected the final unfinished copy. Deliver eligible pending PE interrupts at
the native SDK entry before the existing source critical section/reset.
Preserve genuine GPU completion, original pending one-bit/coalescing, owner
thread, CPU mask, temporary source context, callback, reset and wait behavior.
Do not filter old completions by request generation, add game waits, synthesize
copy readiness or alter the reconstructed game/VI/bitmap/source decisions.

diff --git a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXManage.cpp b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXManage.cpp
--- a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXManage.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXManage.cpp
@@ -292,6 +292,11 @@
 }
 
 void GXSetDrawDone() {
+  // Native safe point for a genuine already-latched PE finish interrupt.
+  // Hardware can deliver it before the original SDK critical section; late
+  // owner polling must not let that old cause satisfy the following reset.
+  // Existing owner/context/mask rules retain pending masked/foreign causes.
+  aurora::gx::fifo::service_draw_done();
   const BOOL enabled = OSDisableInterrupts();
   GX_WRITE_RAS_REG(kDrawDoneCommand);
   GXFlush();
